A||||3||RLMay||Gertrag Backup light switch||||5||
Z||000000||RLMay||07-02-2000||10:36 PM||||Hi to all on this forum.  Iv'e been a reader for some time, but this is my first post.<P>I recently converted my '86 GT 4-spped to a Getrag 5-speed.  Everything went well, except the backup lights don't work.  I've diaganosed the backup light switch as the problem, but none of my manuals discuss the backup light switch.  Has any one had any experience withthe Getrag backup light switch.  Is it adjustable?  Can it be removed without splitting the case?  If so, are there any special tricks.  Thanks for your help.||||reg||5
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||07-02-2000||11:35 PM||||The 4 speed used a lever in the shifter to turn the reverse lights on and the Getrag has it inside the tranny. If you look at the wiring harness for the speedo sensor there should be an 'extra' plug hanging near it. This should plug right into the Getrag's plug for the reverse switch. It may not be there but it was on the last 3 or 4 cars I looked at.<P>------------------<BR>-Chris <BR>88 Fiero Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIEROCIOUS||07-03-2000||02:53 AM||||The switch wire is located directly under the shift mechinism on the trany purple and green (if memory serves) Mine doesn't work either "So how do you fix it any way?"||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bruce||07-03-2000||12:55 PM||||If the shifter doesn't go far enough to the left when you shift into reverse, it won't activate the backup lights. I had to have the shifter cables adjusted in order for the switch to work. If the switch is defective, you can buy one from Kick Hill Farms for about $5.||||reg||1
